---
description: UI/UX rules for the Nuxt PWA.
globs: apps/pwa/**
alwaysApply: true
---

Use these rules when writing frontend UI code.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS is the default; prefer utility classes over custom CSS.
- Consult `apps/pwa/tailwind.config.js` and `apps/pwa/assets/css/tailwind.css` for tokens and base styles before adding new patterns.
- Prefer shadcn-nuxt components for base UI; extend with Tailwind utilities.
- Keep layouts responsive and mobile-friendly.

## Components

- Use semantic HTML in Vue templates.
- Keep components small and focused.
- Avoid inline styles; use Tailwind classes instead.

## Charts

- Use shadcn-vue charts (via shadcn-nuxt) instead of D3/Unovis.
